Ember rewrites of Code-OSS :has() rules into state classes (issues #142, #143, INTENT D23).
The renderer's stylo does not parse :has(), so each rule would be dropped. The chrome rsx sets
the class instead. Applied by ember/ose/vendor-workbench-css.sh with `patch -p1`.

  views.css            .monaco-list-row:has(.actions .action-item)       -> .monaco-list-row.has-actions
                       (3 rules: :hover, .selected, .focused stay as they are)
                       .monaco-list-row:has(.monaco-icon-label:is(.monaco-decoration-itemColor,
                       .monaco-decoration-badge))                        -> .monaco-list-row.has-decoration
                       .viewpane-filter-container:has(input :focus, controls :focus)
                                                                         -> .viewpane-filter-container.is-focused
  titlebarpart.css     .command-center-center:has(.compact-mode)         -> .command-center-center.compact-mode
                       (3 rules)
  actionWidget.css     .action-widget:has(.action-list-header)           -> .action-widget.has-header
                       (derived: the rule tests for a header banner child; the widget sets
                       has-header when it draws one)

diff a/actionWidget.css b/actionWidget.css
